@startuml C02-dual-rejected-status
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title C-02 — Dual-Rejected Status Collision\nTwo distinct outcomes share the same Task.status value

package "Intended meaning" {
  card "Genuinely Rejected" as r1 {
    file "Task.status = rejected\nTask.businessStatus = #rejected\nTask.statusReason.text = \"Full at capacity\"\n\nMeaning: Facility cannot take case.\nNo onward destination given." as t1 #FFCDD2
  }

  card "Referred Onward" as r2 {
    file "Task.status = rejected        ← SAME!\nTask.businessStatus = #referred-onward\nTask.statusReason = #capacity-full\nTask.output → onward SR\n\nMeaning: Facility cannot take case.\nNew destination identified." as t2 #FFE0B2
  }
}

package "FHIR query results" {
  frame "GET Task?status=rejected" as query #E8EAF6 {
    card "Returns BOTH ↑ Tasks" #BBDEFB
  }
}

note bottom of query
  A dashboard counting "rejections"
  includes referred-onward cases.

  A system filtering Task?status=rejected
  cannot distinguish:
    • "Case refused — no alternative"
    • "Case redirected — alternative given"

  without reading businessStatus on every result.

  Reporting impact example (10 tasks):
    Query returns 10 "rejected" tasks.
    Actual breakdown:
      3 genuinely rejected (no path for patient)
      7 referred onward   (patient redirected)

    Dashboard: "Rejection rate: 100%"
    Reality:   "Genuine rejection rate: 30%"
end note

@enduml
